# VoiceKit is a Windows-only AutoHotkey project, but its generators (the AHK
# writers AND mcp/voicekit_writer.py) create files with LF endings, and the
# conformance tests compare against that. So source and data are LF in the
# working tree too; only the Windows batch/PowerShell scripts are CRLF, since
# cmd.exe can misparse labels and GOTOs in an LF .bat/.cmd. Git stores LF.
* text=auto
*.ahk text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Known binary types (none tracked today, but future-proof the shortcuts,
# icons and any recordings/screenshots that might get added).
*.lnk binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
